   "caption_before": [
    "In the validation cohort patients were not matched for gender, follow-up, or BE segment length. In this group we aimed to evaluate a single timepoint from the earliest possible full surveillance endoscopy. In the progressor patients we did have a couple more timepoints as we were not certain that we would have sufficient DNA. However, all of the extra samples passed QC and so were included.",
    "Supplementary Table 3 Model coefficients",
    "Genomic regions selected by the model as being predictive of progression with their associated coefficient of variation for the relative risk (i.e. , where y is the matrix value) and status (i.e. relative gain or loss). Few are strong drivers of the model, and even the top five coefficients are found in relatively few patients or samples. For example, the loss of 17p was not sufficient to predict progression as it occurred in only 9% of all samples (70/773), and while it occurred exclusively in progressor patients it was only in 20% (70/349) of progressor patient samples. Furthermore, due to the nature of elastic-net coefficient selection, these features change as patients are added to the model training process (Supplementary Fig. 6B) indicating that the model is not yet saturated. Many of the features listed in the table above are consistently selected, but the strength of the predictive power in the model () is not stable indicating that the model has not yet converged. The \u2018cx\u2019 coefficient is the value added to the model to represent the overall complexity of the genome."
   ],
